@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-120b-indexation`
IMPORT `ito-121-individual-rates`
IMPORT `ito-121b-additional-tax`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for row IL-03, written by fid-il-03.
-- Every expected value below was decided from the Hebrew source alone and written down in
-- DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (stamped Tue Oct  6 14:02:44 UTC 2026) BEFORE any .l4 file or
-- NOTES.md in this directory was opened. The ids (A01, S07, ...) are that file's ids.
-- A failing assertion here is a finding. No expected value was edited after a run.
--
-- Numbers that are not in the source are inputs I chose:
--   * 721,560 as the s 121B(a) amount: taken from the editorial note only as a convenient
--     value; it is not law (DECIDED-ANSWERS R0.2);
--   * every index reading and every s 120B base amount: hypothetical.
-- The fixtures below are my own; the encoder's tests module is not imported.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Fixtures — items of income`

-- Employment income: s 2(2), from personal exertion, on the s 121 scale.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`wages of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- A pension from a former employer: personal exertion under s 1 def. (1), not s 2(1)/(2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a pension of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Business income (s 2(1)) for which books were required and acceptable books were kept.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`trade income with acceptable books of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Business income (s 2(1)) for which books were required and acceptable books were NOT kept.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`trade income lacking the books it required of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS TRUE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- Rent taxed on the s 121 scale: not personal exertion, not s 2(1)/(2), so a capital source.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`rent on the scale of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- A dividend charged at a rate of its own (not on the s 121 scale): a capital source.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a dividend at its own rate of` n MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0

-- A capital gain of n, of which m is the s 88 inflationary amount.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income`
`a capital gain with an inflationary part` n m MEANS
    `An item of income` WITH
        `amount`                                                               IS n
        `from personal exertion`                                               IS FALSE
        `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS FALSE
        `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS FALSE
        `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS m

§§ `Fixtures — sales of real estate`

GIVEN b  IS A NUMBER
      v  IS A NUMBER
      ex IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a residential sale` b v ex MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS 0
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS TRUE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS v
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS ex

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in real estate`
`a non-residential sale with betterment` b MEANS
    `A sale of a right in real estate` WITH
        `betterment`                                                                    IS b
        `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS 0
        `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS FALSE
        `sale value`                                                                    IS 1_000_000
        `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS FALSE

§§ `Fixtures — individuals`

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      dob   IS A DATE
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      sales IS A LIST OF `A sale of a right in real estate`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`a taxpayer` y dob items sales MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                       IS y
        `date of birth`                  IS dob
        `items of income`                IS items
        `sales of rights in real estate` IS sales

-- Under 60 in every year tested (born 1980).
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`under 60` y items MEANS `a taxpayer` y (YMD 1980 6 15) items (EMPTY)

-- 60 reached well before every year tested (born 1960).
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`over 60` y items MEANS `a taxpayer` y (YMD 1960 3 1) items (EMPTY)

GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      items IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      sales IS A LIST OF `A sale of a right in real estate`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`under 60 with sales` y items sales MEANS `a taxpayer` y (YMD 1980 6 15) items sales

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`s121` i MEANS `the tax under section 121 for` i

-- 121B with my chosen input amount 721,560 (DECIDED-ANSWERS R0.2).
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`s121B at 721,560` i MEANS `the additional tax under section 121B for` i `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` 721_560

