§§ `2 — s 120B indexation`

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
      e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Index readings for a period`
`readings` s e MEANS
    `Index readings for a period` WITH
        `index last published before the start of the period` IS s
        `index last published before the end of the period`   IS e

GIVEN y      IS A NUMBER
      prev   IS A NUMBER
      r      IS AN `Index readings for a period`
      before IS A NUMBER
      after  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
`a ceiling` y prev r before after MEANS
    `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `an income ceiling`
        `tax year`                                                      IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS prev
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS r
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS JUST before
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS after

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `An allowance-point amount in a tax year`
`a pension point of 1,000` y m MEANS
    `An allowance-point amount in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                                    IS y
        `amount on 1 January of the tax year`                         IS 1_000
        `month from which an agreed cost-of-living increment is paid` IS m
        `readings from the start of the tax year to the end of that month` IS `readings` 100 101.5

-- I01-I05: the s 1 arithmetic through s 120B(a).
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 100_000 `by the index over` (`readings` 100 103)   EQUALS 103_000
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 50_000  `by the index over` (`readings` 100 110)   EQUALS 55_000
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 84_120  `by the index over` (`readings` 100 102.5) EQUALS 86_223
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 75_960  `by the index over` (`readings` 100 99.4)  EQUALS 75_504.24
#ASSERT `s 120B(a) — adjust` 75_960  `by the index over` (`readings` 100 100)   EQUALS 75_960
-- I06: the rate alone.
#ASSERT `the rate of increase of the index over` (`readings` 104 106.08) EQUALS 0.02

-- I07-I09: the freeze. The unrounded 2024 figure is set apart from the rounded one on purpose.
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2025 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 193_800
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2026 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 193_800
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2027 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` 193_800
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2025 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS 193_800
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2026 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS 193_800
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2027 200_000 (`readings` 100 104) 193_795.5 193_800) EQUALS 193_800

-- I10: the 2028 restart from the 2024 figure BEFORE rounding, by the 2027 index only.
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2028 84_120 (`readings` 105 107.1) 84_000 84_120) EQUALS `adjusted, before rounding, to` 85_680
-- I11 (caller holds only the rounded 2024 figure): not expressible; the record requires both.
-- I12: 2029, the ordinary (a) adjustment from the 1 January 2028 figure.
#ASSERT `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2029 85_680 (`readings` 107.1 109.242) 84_000 84_120) EQUALS `adjusted, before rounding, to` 87_393.6
-- I13: a rounded adjusted amount is declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2028 84_120 (`readings` 105 107.1) 84_000 84_120)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2029 85_680 (`readings` 107.1 109.242) 84_000 84_120)
-- I14: the 1 January 2024 adjustment (low confidence).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B — the amount for the tax year` (`a ceiling` 2024 80_000 (`readings` 100 103) 84_000 84_120)
-- I15: (b) cost-of-living increment from month 6 of 2029; I16: none in a freeze year.
#ASSERT `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`a pension point of 1,000` 2029 (JUST 6)) EQUALS 1_015
#ASSERT `s 120B(b) — the allowance-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment` (`a pension point of 1,000` 2026 (JUST 6)) EQUALS 1_000

§§ `3 — s 121B, with the s 121B(a) amount supplied as 721,560`

-- S01-S04 thresholds; S05-S08 the (a1) capital limb; S09-S10 what is not capital.
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 721_559))                                               EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 721_560))                                               EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 721_561))                                               EQUALS RIGHT 0.03
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 1_000_000))                                             EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 100_000, `a dividend at its own rate of` 721_560))      EQUALS RIGHT 3_000
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `a dividend at its own rate of` 721_561))                          EQUALS RIGHT 0.05
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `a dividend at its own rate of` 900_000))                          EQUALS RIGHT 8_922
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 500_000, `a dividend at its own rate of` 500_000))      EQUALS RIGHT 8_353.2
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`over 60`  2026 (LIST `a pension of` 900_000))                                           EQUALS RIGHT 5_353.2
#ASSERT `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2026 (LIST `trade income with acceptable books of` 900_000))                  EQUALS RIGHT 5_353.2
-- S11 (no amount supplied -> refuse): not expressible as an assertion; the amount is a
-- required argument of the s 121B rule, so the case cannot be posed. Satisfied by the types.
-- S12 (640,000 used without input): checked by reading, not by assertion; see findings.
-- S13: tax year 2025, amount supplied; S14: tax year 2024.
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2025 (LIST `a dividend at its own rate of` 900_000))                  EQUALS RIGHT 8_922
#ASSERT REFUSED `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60` 2024 (LIST `a dividend at its own rate of` 900_000))

§§ `3A — the s 121B(e) definition of taxable income`

-- S20 s 88 inflationary amount excluded; S21 non-residential betterment included;
-- S22-S24 the residential-apartment limb; S25 the same in 2025; S26 a residential sale in
-- 2027; S27 betterment is capital-source income.
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 700_000, `a capital gain with an inflationary part` 100_000 50_000) (EMPTY)) EQUALS RIGHT 853.2
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a non-residential sale with betterment` 200_000))         EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a residential sale` 200_000 5_385_285 FALSE))            EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a residential sale` 200_000 5_385_286 FALSE))            EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a residential sale` 200_000 6_000_000 TRUE))             EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2025 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a residential sale` 200_000 5_385_286 FALSE))            EQUALS RIGHT 2_353.2
#ASSERT REFUSED `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2027 (LIST `wages of` 600_000) (LIST `a residential sale` 200_000 5_385_286 FALSE))
#ASSERT         `s121B at 721,560` (`under 60 with sales` 2026 (LIST `rent on the scale of` 600_000) (LIST `a non-residential sale with betterment` 200_000)) EQUALS RIGHT 3_922

§§ `3B — provisions with no number`

-- S30: s 91(d) does not apply to income chargeable to the additional tax.
#ASSERT `s 121B(b) — section 91(d) on advance payments applies to income chargeable to additional tax under (a) or (a1)` EQUALS FALSE
